/// Turns an already published post into a paid ad that keeps the post's likes and comments, creating the campaign around it.  By default it provisions the whole hierarchy (campaign, ad set, ad).  ### Attach shape (Meta)  Send `adSetId` to put the ad under an EXISTING ad set instead, so that ad set keeps its learning phase.  That ad set then owns `budget`, `schedule` and `targeting`. Sending any of those alongside `adSetId` is a 400 rather than a silent drop. `budget` is required only without `adSetId`.  `instagramAccountId`, `destinationType`, `whatsappPhoneNumber` and `adSetId` are Meta-only and return 400 on other platforms.  ### Meta accounts  `accountId` may be a Facebook, Instagram or Meta ads (business login) connection.  A business-login connection has no posting account, so pass the post as `platformPostId` (Facebook `pageId_postId` or an Instagram media id). A Zernio `postId` is a 400 there.  ### X  `accountId` may be the posting X account or its X Ads connection: either resolves the other on the same profile.  A Zernio `postId` on an X Ads connection resolves through its X account, and is a 400 when the profile has none (pass `platformPostId` instead).  ### Reddit  `accountId` is the Reddit Ads connection (platform `redditads`). Pass the Reddit post as either:  - `platformPostId` (`t3_abc123` or the bare id) - a Zernio `postId`, which resolves through the Reddit account connected on the same profile (400 when there is none)  Reddit promotes only posts made by a profile of the ad account: a post by any other author returns 422.  Goals:  - traffic - awareness - conversions - video_views (the post must be a video, 422 otherwise) - lead_generation  conversions and lead_generation need a pixel that already received the event (see `promotedObject`).  `leadGenFormId` returns 400: Reddit retired its native lead forms, so `lead_generation` sends people to `linkUrl` and optimizes toward the pixel's Lead event.  Each boost creates a campaign, an ad group carrying the budget, the targeting and the bid, and the ad. `bidStrategy` sets the ad group's bid:  - LOWEST_COST_WITHOUT_CAP (or omitted): automatic bidding (BIDLESS) - LOWEST_COST_WITH_BID_CAP: MANUAL_BIDDING with `bidAmount` as the bid - COST_CAP: MAXIMIZE_VOLUME with `bidAmount` as the cap - Any other strategy returns 422 before anything is created.  ### Messaging boosts (Meta)  Use `goal: engagement` with one of these CTAs:  - `callToAction: WHATSAPP_MESSAGE`: implies WHATSAPP - `MESSAGE_PAGE`: implies MESSENGER - `INSTAGRAM_MESSAGE`: implies INSTAGRAM_DIRECT  `destinationType` alone does not select a messaging CTA. Omit `linkUrl` only for messaging CTAs. Plain link CTAs keep their goal and link behavior when combined with an independent `destinationType`.  The campaign uses OUTCOME_ENGAGEMENT and the ad set uses CONVERSATIONS with the promoted Page. Optional `whatsappPhoneNumber` selects a number already paired with that Page.  Conflicting CTA/destination, instant form, goal, or optimizationGoal inputs return 400. Attach requires the target ad set destination to match.  Existing post references preserve social proof. An Instagram reel rejected by Meta is not re-uploaded as a new post for a messaging boost.  ### Retries  Boosts are NOT idempotent and can take minutes when Meta requires re-hosting an Instagram video, so do not retry on client timeout.  Send an Idempotency-Key header to make retries safe: same key and body replays the original 201, and distinct keys always create distinct ads.  Without the header, an identical request is treated as a retry:  - While one is in flight it returns 409. - Within 10 minutes of a completed boost it returns the already-created ad instead of creating another.  To intentionally duplicate an ad, send distinct Idempotency-Keys (or vary the body, e.g. the name).
