/// Creates a paid ad with your own creative, building the campaign and ad set it needs or adding it to existing ones.  Works across Meta, Google Ads, Pinterest, TikTok, X, LinkedIn, OpenAI Ads (ChatGPT Ads) and Reddit Ads. Per-platform required fields, budget minimums, and video-ad rules are documented on each property below.  ### Request shapes  The body selects one of these mutually exclusive shapes:  - Legacy single-creative shape (all platforms, the default). - Meta-only multi-creative shape via the creatives array: one ad set with N ads sharing budget and targeting. - Attach shape via adSetId: adds one new ad to an existing ad set, inheriting its budget, targeting, and schedule (Meta, Google Ads, TikTok, and LinkedIn).  On LinkedIn, adSetId in the attach shape is the existing Campaign id, and the budget, schedule, targeting and bidding fields must be omitted. `goal` may be omitted too (taken from the Campaign's objective), and the created ad's `targeting` echoes the Campaign's audience.  ### Google Performance Max  Set `campaignType: \"pmax\"` and supply `assetGroup` with text, images by role, business name and finalUrl. This creates a daily budget, PAUSED campaign and asset group atomically.  - `validateOnly: true` validates the complete request with Google without creating or persisting resources. - Read assets with `GET /v1/ads/campaigns/{campaignId}/asset-groups`. - The logo is required; video is optional via `assetGroup.youtubeVideoId`. - Brand guidelines are disabled at creation. - All supplied asset links are validated together against Google's minimum asset requirements. - PMax rejects ACTIVE creation, portfolio bidding, bid caps, legacy creative fields and attach shapes. - Geo and language targeting are supported; omitted geo targets all locations. - PMax does not require top-level goal, headline, body or linkUrl.  Supported bidding:  - Omitted or LOWEST_COST_WITHOUT_CAP: Maximize Conversions. - COST_CAP plus bidAmount: target CPA. - LOWEST_COST_WITH_MIN_ROAS plus roasAverageFloor: Maximize Conversion Value with target ROAS.  ### Google Demand Gen  Set `campaignType: \"demand_gen\"` and supply `demandGen`. One atomic request creates a daily budget, PAUSED campaign, one ad group and one ad. The ad is:  - a multi-asset image ad by default; - a video responsive ad when `demandGen.youtubeVideoIds` is sent; - a carousel ad (2 to 10 cards) when `demandGen.carouselCards` is sent.  Targeting and validation:  - Geo (countries, regions, cities, zips, metros) and languages go on the ad group, as Demand Gen requires. - `demandGen.channels` sets the ad group's channel controls. - `demandGen.audience` builds a Google Audience (user lists, interests, custom audiences, age ranges, genders) attached to the ad group, or `demandGen.audienceId` attaches an existing one. - `validateOnly: true` validates everything with Google without creating resources.  Supported bidding:  - Omitted or LOWEST_COST_WITHOUT_CAP: Maximize Conversions. - COST_CAP plus bidAmount: target CPA. - LOWEST_COST_WITH_MIN_ROAS plus roasAverageFloor: target ROAS. - LOWEST_COST_WITH_BID_CAP plus bidAmount: target CPC.  The created ad carries the native `platformCampaignId`, `platformAdSetId` (ad group) and `platformAdId`. After creation:  - Activate with PUT /v1/ads/campaigns/{campaignId}/status. - Edit budget, bidding and name with the regular campaign endpoints. - Edit creative, channels, audience and ad group targeting with PUT /v1/ads/{adId} (`demandGen`, `targeting`).  To grow an existing Demand Gen campaign, send one of these (neither takes budget, bidding or schedule fields; both support `validateOnly`):  - `existingCampaignId`: adds a PAUSED ad group, with its own geo, languages, channels and audience, plus its ad. - `adSetId`: adds a PAUSED ad to that ad group.  ### Meta creative options  Meta accepts `creativeFeatures` on the single and attach shapes and as defaults for `creatives[]`; an item replaces the whole feature map.  `promotion` is not supported on any shape, and any object is rejected with 400.  Reusing `existingCreativeId` uses the existing creative settings instead of new settings. Requested settings are persisted for lists, exports, and default ad-detail reads.  ### Meta required fields per shape  A missing field is a 400 naming it in `param`.  - Every shape that builds a new ad set (no `adSetId`, `existingCampaignId` or `buyingType: \"RESERVED\"`): `budgetAmount`. `budgetType` defaults to daily, and a lifetime budget without `endDate` ends 7 days after it starts (see `appliedDefaults`). - Single image or video (the default), also with `adSetId`: `headline` (max 255), `body`, `callToAction`, and exactly one of `imageUrl` / `video`. A catalog template creative takes none, and ignores and does not upload any sent. - Single image or video also needs `linkUrl`, unless the goal is `lead_generation` or `page_visits` or `leadGenFormId` is set. - `bodies[]` / `headlines[]` text variations: `body`, one list with 2+ items, `callToAction`, `imageUrl` or `video`, and `linkUrl` unless the goal is `lead_generation` or `leadGenFormId` is set. `headline` is not required. - `placementAssets`: `headline`, `body`, `callToAction`, and `linkUrl` with the same exemptions as the single shape; the media comes from `placementAssets`. - `carouselCards`: `body`, `callToAction`, and `linkUrl` unless the goal is `lead_generation` or `leadGenFormId` is set. `headline` is not required. - `creatives[]`: per entry `headline`, `body`, `callToAction`, `imageUrl` or `video`, and `linkUrl` unless the goal is `lead_generation`. Top-level `body` is not required. - `dynamicCreative`: `imageUrls` or `videoUrls`, `callToActionTypes`, and `linkUrls` unless the goal is `lead_generation`. Top-level `body` is not required. - `existingCreativeId`: no creative fields. - Goal `page_likes`: `body` only. - Goal `lead_generation` always needs `leadGenFormId`, except with `existingCreativeId`.  ### Meta activation  Meta builds the campaign, ad set and ads PAUSED and switches the requested levels to ACTIVE as the last step.  When Meta refuses that switch, or the connection drops, after Zernio's retries, the request still answers 201 and nothing is deleted:  - The refused level and every level below it stay PAUSED. - Levels above it that already went ACTIVE stay ACTIVE. - The ad comes back with `status: paused` and its `configuredStatus` as read back from Meta. - A switch Meta applied although its answer was lost counts as ACTIVE, since Zernio reads the status back first.  `message` says not everything is ACTIVE. `warnings` carries one entry starting with `activation_failed:` that quotes Meta's code, subcode and message, and names what was kept PAUSED and what was switched ACTIVE.  That warning also lists the calls that switch the PAUSED ones on later, in this order, with status `active`:  1. PUT /v1/ads/campaigns/{campaignId}/status 2. PUT /v1/ads/ad-sets/{adSetId}/status 3. PUT /v1/ads/{adId}/status  On the `creatives[]` shape, only the ads Meta refused stay PAUSED when the campaign and ad set went through. A Reach and Frequency ad is created ACTIVE and is never listed as kept PAUSED. With an `Idempotency-Key`, a retry replays this 201.  ### LinkedIn  LinkedIn creates a Single Image or Single Video Ad backed by a Direct Sponsored Content \"dark post\" authored by a Company Page (see `organizationId`).  - Supported goals: engagement, traffic, awareness, and video_views. - Video ads use the `video` field; video_views requires a video. - Traffic ads require `linkUrl`.  ### Reddit Ads  Use the `accountId` of a `redditads` connection and an `adAccountId` like `a2_abc123`. Zernio creates a campaign, an ad group carrying the budget, schedule, targeting and pixel, and an ad running a new promoted post. The post is authored by the ad account's first profile (422 when it has none).  The creative format follows the body:  - `carouselCards`: a carousel. - `video`: a video ad. - `imageUrl`: an image ad. - None of them: a text ad, which cannot link out (`linkUrl` is a 400 there; `body` is required).  Only the legacy single-creative shape is available: `creatives[]`, `adSetId`, `existingCampaignId` and `validateOnly` are refused.  Reddit throttling surfaces as 429 `rate_limited` with `platform: reddit`; retry after a delay. To promote an existing Reddit post, use POST /v1/ads/boost.  ### Idempotency  This endpoint is not idempotent at the platform level: a blind retry creates a second campaign/ad set/ad. Send an `Idempotency-Key` header to make retries safe.  - The first request with a given key creates the ad and we store the response. - A retry with the same key replays that exact response (with `Idempotent-Replayed: true`) instead of creating duplicates. - Reusing a key with a different body returns 422. - A key whose first request is still in flight returns 409 (retry after a short backoff). - If the first request is cut off mid-create (for example by a function timeout), its key can stay in progress and keep returning 409 until it expires. Use a new key to retry sooner, after checking whether the ad was created. - Keys are scoped to your credential and expire after 24h.
