/// Deletes a campaign on its platform, including a campaign that never got any ads.  Only the campaign itself is sent to the platform:  - Meta, Google, TikTok, LinkedIn and X delete it. - OpenAI, Reddit and Pinterest have no campaign delete and archive it instead (see below).  Locally, all Ad documents for this campaign are marked `status: cancelled`.  ### Empty campaigns  A campaign with zero ads has no local Ad documents to resolve, so it is invisible to `/v1/ads/tree` and this endpoint would 404. That state comes from the two-step create flow (campaign, then ads via `existingCampaignId`) whenever Meta rejects the ad step.  To delete such a shell, send `accountId` in the body or the query string. We skip the local lookup entirely and forward the delete to the platform of that connection. `accountId` is ignored when the campaign does have ads.  ### Google, TikTok, LinkedIn, Pinterest, Reddit and OpenAI  Google, TikTok, LinkedIn, Pinterest and Reddit take the ad account from the synced campaign (OpenAI needs none). When the campaign was never synced (or is synced under several ad accounts), the answer is 409 `invalid_resource_state` on `campaignId` and nothing is deleted: sync the ad account and retry.  Before deleting on Google, TikTok, LinkedIn, Pinterest, OpenAI or Reddit, Zernio asks the platform whether the campaign still holds ad groups or ads. Google asset groups count; on LinkedIn, campaigns inside the campaign group count.  If it does, or the platform cannot confirm it has none (a TikTok Smart+ campaign), the answer is 409 `invalid_resource_state` on `campaignId` and nothing is deleted. Either:  - sync the ad account and delete the campaign again so its ads are cancelled with it, or - delete them on the platform first.  ### X  On X the ad account comes from the synced campaign, which wins over `adAccountId`. When the campaign was never synced, send `adAccountId` too.  Before deleting, Zernio asks X whether the campaign still holds undeleted line items (ads